  <div class="container">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>Project scope, methodology, editorial policy, and what this archive does and does not seek to do.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="container">
  <div class="prose">

    <p>
      ALPR Nebraska is an independent public-interest archive of public records concerning
      governmental automated license plate reader systems in Nebraska. The project collects and
      publishes source documents, records-request correspondence, and neutral summaries concerning
      policy, procurement, deployment, statutory reporting, data retention, information sharing,
      and oversight. It is not currently a 501(c)(3) charitable organization and does not accept
      tax-deductible contributions.
    </p>

    <h2>In scope</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Municipal police departments.</li>
      <li>County sheriff's offices.</li>
      <li>City and county governing bodies.</li>
      <li>City/county procurement, finance, IT, traffic, public works, parking, and records offices.</li>
      <li>Nebraska Crime Commission annual-report materials.</li>
      <li>Nebraska Department of Transportation agreements and right-of-way records.</li>
      <li>Nebraska State Patrol and other state-agency use or sharing arrangements.</li>
      <li>Public-university police departments where they operate or access ALPR systems.</li>
      <li>Governmental or quasi-governmental entities only when they operate, fund, host, access, or materially govern the system.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Out of scope</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Raw plate-read databases, individual plates, images, location histories, or other protected personal/investigative data.</li>
      <li>Private businesses' ALPR systems, <em>unless</em> there is a government contract, data-sharing agreement, procurement relationship, or governmental access arrangement.</li>
      <li>Unverified reports or social-media claims presented as factual findings.</li>
      <li>General surveillance issues unrelated to ALPR, at least until the core archive has a sustainable workflow.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Editorial and correction policy</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Primary documents are preferred over secondary accounts.</li>
      <li>Claims must identify the source document and the specific supporting page, row, or section.</li>
      <li>Agency statements are labeled as agency statements.</li>
      <li>"No record located" means no record was located through the described search — not proof a program does not exist.</li>
      <li>Corrections are dated and visible.</li>
      <li>Submissions may be rejected for lack of provenance, relevance, privacy concerns, or inability to verify.</li>
      <li>The project does not publish personal ALPR capture data, plate numbers, individual location histories, or sensitive investigative details.</li>
      <li>Contributors retain responsibility for lawful acquisition and submission of materials.</li>
      <li>The project may redact or decline to publish material that creates unnecessary privacy or safety risk.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Statutory background</h2>
    <p>
      Nebraska enacted ALPR-specific legislation governing agency use, retention, and reporting.
      Key statutes:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Neb. Rev. Stat. §§ 84-712–84-712.09</strong> — Nebraska Public Records Act. Under § 84-712(4), a records custodian must, within four business days, provide responsive records, issue a written denial stating the legal basis, or notify the requester that additional time is needed and provide an estimated completion date and cost.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Neb. Rev. Stat. § 60-3206</strong> — Requires agencies operating ALPR systems to
        file annual practice and usage reports with the Nebraska Crime Commission.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Neb. Rev. Stat. § 60-3209</strong> — Provides that captured ALPR data held by a governmental entity is not a public record, subject to the statute’s terms and exceptions. Accordingly, this project does not seek to publish raw ALPR captures, individual plate information, or associated personal/investigative data.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Other inquiries</h2>
    <p>
      For general questions about the project, press inquiries, or information requests not
      covered by the <a href="/contributing/">contributing page</a>, contact
      <a href="mailto:info@alprnebraska.org">info@alprnebraska.org</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy & Site Stats</h2>
    <p>
      ALPR Nebraska uses a self-hosted, cookie-free analytics service to collect aggregate site-usage metrics. It does not use advertising identifiers, cross-site tracking, or persistent visitor profiles. Routine web-server access logs are not retained for analytics purposes.
    </p>

